## opencode specifics

- **Skills and agents** — the rolepod skills install at
  `~/.config/opencode/skills/<name>/` and auto-trigger from their
  `description:`; 4 agent types install at `~/.config/opencode/agents/*.md`
  and run by description or `@<name>`, each carrying its own protocol.
- **Tier classes** — map cheap / balanced / strong ONCE per session onto the
  models the user has opted into (configured providers), never the whole
  aggregator catalog; a rung costlier than anything configured is a cost
  decision to surface. Cheap = small / fast, balanced = mid flagship,
  strong = the set's top reasoning model. Cannot classify →
  balanced, and say so.
- **workflow.mode** — Lite / Standard / Full never change which gates hold. The private-docs deny runs on every CLI and the sub-agent commit ban on Codex and opencode; review / test evidence, cannot-wait, sibling-edit and fan-out gates are Claude-only. Nothing else is mechanically enforced here — never report it as such.
